<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 379 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 379 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 379 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN    1.1 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    250 MLN    360 MLN    739 MLN    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BILL/FRG TO FEB 3    250 MLN!   =	    =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1 T-BILLS	 =	    =	    100 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS    =	    =	    279 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS    =	    110 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE OF 5-15/16 (IDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INTEREST RATE OF 5-31/32 PCT(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
